From 1fe717c82e3744c7e2af048bf017691d3419ab19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 08:56:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Emscripten: fibers as baton-passing pthreads

WebAssembly cannot switch stacks, so each fiber runs on its own pthread and
Fiber::Switch hands control over with a semaphore. Thread-locals that belong to
the emulated core (assigned core, scheduler fiber, scheduler lock count, current
PPC instance) become CEMU_FIBER_LOCAL and are handed over on every switch.
The scheduler lock is held across fiber switches, so on Emscripten it is an
ownerless lock instead of a recursive pthread mutex.
